			<div class="content" id="post-content-2145680">
									

<p>I'm afraid this doesn't appeal to me.</p>
<p>I respect the high concept, but in general, articles that only make sense because of an on-the-nose line in a final interview seem a little played out to me — I prefer interviews that add to a concept that stands on its own, and this doesn't. Why are the entities superpowered?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>which had previously been [DATA EXPUNGED] due to its memetic effects</p>
</blockquote>
<p>There's a lot of redactions like this that don't add anything. I would focus on making the writing of higher-concept articles like this breezier and more accessible.</p>
<p>-1.</p>

