			<div class="content" id="post-content-2146734">
									

<p>I get where you're coming from, and there's definitely something to be said for bluntness and brevity, but personally I favor the cryptic and arcane articles. A light breezy article that just hands the idea to you is good for a momentary chill or gee whiz!, but the ones that always stick with me are the convoluted ones that take you on a trip down the rabbit hole or that you have to think about for a while before the &quot;Wait a second&#8230;o_o;&quot; really hits you.</p>
<p>Its sort of like eating shelled sunflower seeds or shrimp; having to work at a little before you can get at the good part makes it taste all the better, and is actually part of the appeal.</p>

